index e661c08328..efa88d34bf 100644
--- a/Benchmarks/CPUThroughput/README.md
+++ b/Benchmarks/CPUThroughput/README.md
@@ -200,3 +200,17 @@ python3 Benchmarks/CPUThroughput/compare.py \
 ```
 
 Apple documents P-only counters in [Recount](https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/xnu/blob/f6217f891ac0bb64f3d375211650a4c1ff8ca1ea/doc/observability/recount.md). The [Apple Silicon scheduling guidance](https://developer.apple.com/news/?id=vk3m204o) explains how QoS influences placement. These controls do not expose a public P/E affinity mask.
+
+## Separate compute placement from observation scheduling
+
+Add `--observer-isolation` to `compare_e_cores.py` to select `e-core-workers-observer-v2`. Without the flag, the launcher retains `e-core-application-v1` and its whole-tree clamp.
+
+The new profile backgrounds each compute worker, including preflight and postflight workers. The controller runs without that clamp. Queue dispatch, response collection, memory sampling, and bookkeeping can therefore use either core type. Every timed worker must still record zero P-core user time. Controller P/E time appears separately, and all measured controller CPU remains charged. Raw controller QoS counters reject execution under a background, maintenance, or utility policy.
+
+The new controller charge interval starts before initial worker stats and observations. It ends after the final memory scan, worker stats, counter reads, and receipt validation. Final receipt serialization and disk writes are outside that interval. Queue wall timing retains its original boundaries. Receipts preserve both intervals. The two profiles measure different controller scheduling and charging scopes, so their performance results are not interchangeable.
+
+The sampler uses absolute monotonic deadlines with a requested 10 ms interval. It skips missed deadlines instead of issuing catch-up bursts. Each scan records its start, end, worker identities, RSS, and physical footprint. The independent audit requires boundary scans around the queue, unchanged process start identities, and an exact match between scan RSS and the existing RSS sample list.
+
+Coverage requires every queue to have an effective gap no greater than 50 ms and every scan to take no longer than 50 ms. A coverage failure prevents qualification and remains visible in the raw receipts and audit. This is a measurement-quality limit, not a scheduling guarantee or proof of the instantaneous memory peak.
+
+Physical footprint supplements RSS. It does not replace sampled peak RSS or its repeatability control. Reusable memory is not available through this unprivileged cross-process probe. The work totals, native pools, engine panel, twins, output checks, memory ceiling, and CPU, elapsed-time, and RSS allowances are unchanged. A smoke run cannot qualify comparative performance.
